---
import BaseLayout from '../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={"History and Relaunch — Auspicious Music"}
  description={"What Auspicious Music is today, what was published at this address before 2026, and where the line between the two runs."}
  canonicalPath={"/about/history-and-relaunch/"}
  lang={"en"}
  noindex={false}
  loadStringField={false}
>
<Fragment slot="head">
<style is:global>
@layer components {
  .hist-head { padding-block: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem) clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); }
  .hist-head h1 { max-width: 14ch; margin-top: 1.25rem; }
  .hist-head .lede { margin-top: 1.5rem; max-width: 56ch; }

  .hist-body { max-width: var(--measure); }
  .hist-body > * + * { margin-top: 1.5rem; }
  .hist-body h2 {
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 1.2rem + 1.2vw, 2rem); letter-spacing: -0.016em;
    margin-top: clamp(2.75rem, 5vw, 3.75rem);
  }
  .hist-body p { color: var(--ink-soft); }
  .hist-body a:not(.link) { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }

  /* The disclosure is the load-bearing element of this page: graphite, wide,
     unmissable, and never softened into a decorative panel. */
  .disclosure { padding-block: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); }
  .disclosure p {
    font-size: clamp(1.25rem, 1.05rem + 0.7vw, 1.625rem);
    line-height: 1.5; letter-spacing: -0.011em;
    max-width: 40ch; color: var(--dark-text);
  }
  .disclosure p + p {
    font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.65; letter-spacing: 0;
    color: var(--dark-muted); max-width: 54ch; margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }

  .timeline { position: relative; padding-left: 2rem; }
  .timeline::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: 3px; top: 1.2rem; bottom: 1.2rem;
    width: 1px; background: var(--line-strong);
  }
  .timeline li { position: relative; padding-block: 1.125rem; }
  .timeline li + li { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .timeline li::before {
    content: ""; position: absolute; left: -2rem; top: 1.7rem;
    inline-size: 7px; block-size: 7px; border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--canvas); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px var(--line-strong);
  }
  .timeline li:last-child::before { background: var(--ember-bright); box-shadow: none; }
  .timeline time {
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
    letter-spacing: var(--tr-meta); color: var(--muted);
    display: block; margin-bottom: 0.375rem;
  }
  .timeline h3 { font-size: 1.125rem; letter-spacing: -0.011em; margin-bottom: 0.375rem; }
  .timeline p { color: var(--ink-soft); font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 58ch; }

  .corrections {
    margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem);
    border-left: 2px solid var(--line-strong);
    padding: 0.25rem 0 0.25rem 1.5rem;
  }
  .corrections strong { display: block; margin-bottom: 0.5rem; }
  .corrections p { color: var(--ink); font-size: 1.0625rem; line-height: 1.65; max-width: 56ch; }

  .sources { margin-top: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); padding-top: 2rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .sources h2 { font-size: var(--t-h3); margin-bottom: 1.25rem; margin-top: 0; }
  .sources ol { display: grid; gap: 0.875rem; counter-reset: src; }
  .sources li {
    counter-increment: src; padding-left: 2rem; position: relative;
    font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--muted);
  }
  .sources li::before {
    content: counter(src); position: absolute; left: 0;
    font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: var(--t-meta);
  }
  .sources a { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; text-underline-offset: 3px; }
}
</style>
</Fragment>

<main id="content">

  <section class="hist-head" data-od-id="history-head">
    <div class="shell">
      <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
        <ol>
          <li><a href="/">Home</a></li>
          <li><a href="/about/">About</a></li>
          <li>History &amp; relaunch</li>
        </ol>
      </nav>
      <h1>History and relaunch</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        What Auspicious Music is today, what was published at this address before 2026,
        and exactly where the line between the two runs.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band-dark disclosure" data-od-id="ownership-disclosure">
    <div class="shell">
      <p>
        Auspicious Music was relaunched under new ownership in 2026 as an independent
        publication. Historical references are preserved for context.
      </p>
      <p>
        The current publication does not represent the former operator and makes no
        claim to their work, clients, credits, releases or partnerships. Nothing here
        should be read as endorsed by them unless it is explicitly stated with their
        permission.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="band" data-od-id="history-body">
    <div class="shell">
      <div class="hist-body">

        <h2 style="margin-top:0">The publication today</h2>
        <p>
          Auspicious Music publishes practical guides for music production, Ableton Live
          and Max for Live, sound design and sampling, recording acoustic instruments and
          strings, and composing and delivering music for film, video and events.
        </p>
        <p>
          Every technical page states the software version it was tested against and the
          date of that test. Where something was not tested, the page says so. The
          <a href="/publishing-roadmap/">editorial policy</a> sets out how that works, including the use of
          AI assistance, how corrections are handled, and how any commercial relationship
          is disclosed.
        </p>

        <h2>What was here before</h2>
        <p>
          Between roughly 2013 and 2017 this domain hosted a music-technology site run by
          a different operator, covering Ableton Live and Push, Max for Live devices,
          sampled instruments, controller mappings and production workflows. Several of
          those resources — The Spy Guitar, Bang My Twister and others — were widely
          referenced and are still linked from external pages today.
        </p>
        <p>
          After that period the site stopped being maintained, and the domain was
          subsequently used to host injected spam pages that had nothing to do with music.
          That is a common fate for a lapsed domain with real links pointing at it.
        </p>

        <h2>How the relaunch handles all of that</h2>
        <p>
          Three rules, applied without exception:
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Historic addresses that carried real intent stay answerable.</strong>
          Where someone following a decade-old link was looking for a specific resource,
          they reach a page about that resource — documented as history, with its rights
          position stated and a current alternative offered where one exists. They are
          not silently redirected to the homepage.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Nothing is reissued without the right to reissue it.</strong> The former
          operator's files, text, audio and images did not transfer with the domain. None
          of it is republished here. The <a href="/download/">downloads page</a> lists
          every historic file with its actual status rather than a broken button.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Injected spam paths are removed, not redirected.</strong> Confirmed
          hacked and gambling-spam addresses return a permanent removal response, and
          unknown addresses return an ordinary not-found page. There is no catch-all
          redirect, because a catch-all would pass that history straight into the new
          publication.
        </p>

        <h2>Timeline</h2>
        <ul class="timeline" data-reveal-group>
          <li data-reveal>
            <time datetime="2013">2013 – 2017</time>
            <h3>Previous site active</h3>
            <p>Music-technology publishing under the former operator: Ableton coverage, Max for Live devices, sampled instruments and controller mappings.</p>
          </li>
          <li data-reveal>
            <time datetime="2017">After 2017</time>
            <h3>Site no longer maintained</h3>
            <p>Publishing stops. Over the following years the address is exploited for injected spam pages unrelated to music.</p>
          </li>
          <li data-reveal>
            <time datetime="2026-02">February 2026</time>
            <h3>Domain acquired by the current publisher</h3>
            <p>Historic addresses audited against archive records and backlink data. Spam paths identified and marked for permanent removal.</p>
          </li>
          <li data-reveal>
            <time datetime="2026-08">August 2026</time>
            <h3>Independent relaunch</h3>
            <p>Auspicious Music relaunches as an independent publication with new editorial work and a documented archive layer.</p>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <div class="corrections">
          <strong>Corrections and contact</strong>
          <p>
            If something on this site is wrong — a technical claim, a date, a historical
            detail, or an attribution — write to us and it gets corrected with the change
            recorded on the page. That applies with particular force to anything
            concerning the former operator's work.
          </p>
          <p style="margin-top:1rem">
            <a class="link" href="/publishing-roadmap/">Contact
              <svg viewBox="0 0 14 14" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 7h10M8 3l4 4-4 4" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
            </a>
          </p>
        </div>

        <section class="sources">
          <h2>Sources</h2>
          <ol>
            <li>Internet Archive Wayback Machine — captures of this domain, 2013 onward.</li>
            <li><a href="https://maps.djtechtools.com/mappings/2929" rel="noopener">DJ TechTools mapping archive</a> — independent record of one of the historic projects.</li>
            <li>Internal URL registry — the single source for every redirect and status code on this domain, maintained alongside the site.</li>
          </ol>
        </section>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</main>
</BaseLayout>